% Problem: Comparing tspan Formats for a Sedative Washout Curve
% Name:
% Date:

clear; clc;

k = 0.25;
f = @(t, C) -k * C;
C0 = 6;

% a) Solve with tspan = [0 12]; display length(t1)


% b) Solve with tspan = 0:1:12; display length(t2)


% c) One-line comment explaining the length difference

solutionCode:
k = 0.25;
f = @(t, C) -k * C;
C0 = 6;

% a) Two-element tspan -- solver picks its own time points
tspan1 = [0 12];
[t1, C1] = ode45(f, tspan1, C0);
disp(length(t1))

% b) Explicit tspan vector -- solver reports only at these times
tspan2 = 0:1:12;
[t2, C2] = ode45(f, tspan2, C0);
disp(length(t2))

% c) length(t1) and length(t2) differ because [0 12] lets ode45's adaptive
% step-size algorithm choose however many internal points it needs, while
% 0:1:12 forces it to report the solution at exactly those 13 requested hours.

